%I A395685 #59 Aug 20 2026 03:38:51
%S A395685 1,1,2,4,2,16,8,32,64,24,128,320,224,48,768,2048,1664,512,48,6144,
%T A395685 16384,13312,4096,384,12288,75776,141312,101376,29440,2688,49152,
%U A395685 376832,1019904,1253376,726016,187392,16128,294912,2506752,8003584,12619776,10622976,4754432,1033728,80640
%N A395685 Triangle read by rows: T(0,0) = 1; for k != 0, T(0,k) = 0; T(n,k) = T(n-1,k-1)*b(n) + T(n-1,k)*(n-b(n)) where b(n) = 2^ceiling(log_2(n)) - n.
%C A395685 The triangle of numbers of permutations of length n and the number of comparisons t = tmax - k, where tmax corresponds to A001855, obtained when sorting by binary insertion.
%C A395685 The sequence b(n) gives the number of leaves at the penultimate level in a binary comparison tree with n leaves equals A035327(n-1) for n>=2.
%H A395685 Alois P. Heinz, <a href="/A395685/b395685.txt">Rows n = 0..150, flattened</a> (first 31 rows from Alexander Krivilev)
%H A395685 Alexander Krivilev, <a href="/A395685/a395685_1.png">Plot of a(n) for n = 0..86 (Row 0..15).</a>
%H A395685 A. V. Krivilev and E. O. Gavrichenko, <a href="https://journals.rcsi.science/0132-3474/article/view/437980">Analysis of the Binary Insertion Sort Algorithm and Its Modification Based on Comparison Forests</a>, Programming / Programming and computer software. 2026;1:40-59. (In Russian)
%e A395685 Triangle begins
%e A395685   n\k |     0      1      2      3      4      5
%e A395685   ----+-----------------------------------------
%e A395685    0  |     1
%e A395685    1  |     1
%e A395685    2  |     2
%e A395685    3  |     4      2
%e A395685    4  |    16      8
%e A395685    5  |    32     64     24
%e A395685    6  |   128    320    224     48
%e A395685    7  |   768   2048   1664    512     48
%e A395685    8  |  6144  16384  13312   4096    384
%e A395685    9  | 12288  75776 141312 101376  29440   2688
%e A395685   ...
%p A395685 T:= proc(n,k) option remember; `if`(n=0, `if`(k=0,1,0),
%p A395685       (b-> T(n-1, k-1)*b+T(n-1, k)*(n-b))(2^ceil(log[2](n))-n))
%p A395685     end:
%p A395685 seq(seq(T(n, k), k=0..n-ceil(log[2](n+1))), n=0..11);  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Jul 29 2026
%t A395685 p[n_, x_] := Product[i + (2^Ceiling[Log2[i]] - i) (x - 1), {i, 2, n}]; Table[CoefficientList[Expand@p[k, "x"], "x"], {k, 0, 11}] // Flatten
%Y A395685 Column k=0 gives A398374.
%Y A395685 Row sums give A000142.
%Y A395685 Row lengths are A182220(n+1).
%Y A395685 For n>1, b(n) gives A035327.
%Y A395685 Cf. A261125, A061168.
